            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for an arrow, then the Hindi for for the most part."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: हराना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हराना — harānā — \"to defeat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "छोटी सेना ने बड़ी सेना को हराया। choṭī senā ne baṛī senā ko harāyā. The small army defeated the big one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने दुश्मन को हराया, usne duśman ko harāyā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "हराना (harānā) is the causative partner of हारना, to lose, and CDIAL 14061 lists both under Sanskrit hārayati: to make the other side lose."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
