          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "संधि (sandhi) is Sanskrit saṁdhi, \"a joining, an agreement\" (Monier-Williams). Grammar uses the same word for the joining of sounds; history uses it for the joining of two sides."
            }
          ]
        },
